<!-- SABAS-SECURE-DEVELOPMENT:START -->
## Secure development gate

- For executable changes, load and follow `sabas-secure-qa` before considering the work complete.
- Use risk classes R0-R4 and let the review mode escalate automatically.
- Treat auth, authorization, roles, sessions, admin, sensitive APIs, uploads, SQL, webhooks, payments, secrets, cryptography, multi-tenant behavior, CI/CD and command execution as high-risk surfaces.
- Never report an unavailable security check as passed; mark it `NOT VERIFIED`.
- Confirm server-side authorization and resource ownership for sensitive actions.
- Do not close introduced/affected confirmed or high-confidence Critical/High findings without remediation or explicit documented risk acceptance.
- Run `usuario-torpe-qa` only in an explicitly authorized local/sandbox/staging environment and keep its audit separate from remediation.
- For R2+ changes, immediately before final output rerun `security_context.py` and include exactly one `SABAS_SECURITY_VERDICT` line plus the current `SABAS_SECURITY_FINGERPRINT`.
<!-- SABAS-SECURE-DEVELOPMENT:END -->
